/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 417 0 R
/T (top / left / right / bottom are calculated relative to the first non-static ancestor \(relative, absolute, fixed, or sticky\). If no such ancestor exists, it anchors to the viewport, which often results in a hard-coded, non-responsive layout because the element is positioned against the entire page instead of a flexible container)
/E (top / left / right / bottom are calculated relative to the first non-static ancestor \(relative, absolute, fixed, or sticky\). If no such ancestor exists, it anchors to the viewport, which often results in a hard-coded, non-responsive layout because the element is positioned against the entire page instead of a flexible container)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
